---
import { facts } from '../data/facts';
---

<section id="about">
  <div class="sec-head">
    <div class="sec-num"><b>§ 01</b> &nbsp;— About</div>
    <h2 class="sec-title">A little <em>about</em> me,<br />in plain prose.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="about-body">
    <div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm an <b>AI engineer</b> working at the intersection of <b>language models</b>, <b>agents</b>, and
        <b>retrieval</b> — the end-to-end parts of building systems that
        <span class="hi">need to stay useful after the demo ends</span>. Currently at <b>MNC Group</b>;
        previously at Analitica, where I built <i>Ica</i>, a multi-agent tutor that served five thousand
        students a month.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm drawn to the quiet plumbing: long-term memory, function-calling, and the small act of getting a
        model to say <i>"I don't know"</i> when it should. Most of my favorite days look like evals, retrieval
        pipelines, and the slow work that makes a system feel <i>honest</i> rather than clever.
      </p>
      <p>
        Based in Jakarta. I came up through ESG data work at <b>Astra</b> and sustainability ML at
        <b>CESGS</b>, then studied Data Science at <b>Universitas Airlangga</b>, where I led a small research
        community called IRIS. Co-author of a short paper on RAG for university chatbots
        (<i>KST 2024</i>).
      </p>

      <dl class="fact-list">
        {
          facts.map((f) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{f.key}</dt>
              <dd>{f.value}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
